@startuml
title UC3.2: Send Notification for Job Failure

hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #475569
  GroupBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  GroupBorderColor #475569
}

participant "Job Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
queue "Notification Queue" as Queue
participant "Notification Handler" as Handler
database "Notification\nPreferences Store" as Preferences
database "Notification Store" as Store
participant "Channel Adapter" as Adapter
participant "External Provider" as Provider

Orchestrator ->> Queue: Enqueue failure notification\n(UserId, JobId, FailureDetails)
Queue ->> Handler: Consume notification request
Handler -> Preferences: Load preferences (UserId, JobId)
Preferences --> Handler: Enabled channels and destinations\n(configured through UC3.1)

alt No enabled channels
  Handler -> Store: Record overall outcome: Skipped
else One or more enabled channels
  loop For each enabled channel (sequentially)
    Handler -> Store: Create pending channel notification\n(UserId, JobId, channel, FailureDetails)
    Store --> Handler: NotificationId
    Handler -> Handler: Resolve adapter and validate destination

    alt Missing destination or unsupported adapter
      Handler -> Store: Record channel Failure\n(NotificationId, configuration error)
    else Adapter and destination available
      Handler -> Handler: Prepare common failure message
      Handler -> Adapter: Send (destination, failure message)
      Adapter -> Adapter: Format message for this channel
      Adapter -> Provider: Send via channel-specific provider API
      Provider --> Adapter: Accepted or error
      Adapter --> Handler: Success or Failure (error details)

      alt Provider accepted the message
        Handler -> Store: Record channel Success (NotificationId)
      else Send failed
        Handler -> Store: Record channel Failure\n(NotificationId, error details)
      end
    end

    note over Handler, Store
      Each channel gets a result.
      A failure does not stop the next channel.
    end note
  end

  Handler -> Handler: Aggregate channel results
  note right of Handler
    All succeeded: Success
    Some succeeded: Partial Failure
    None succeeded: Failure
  end note
  Handler -> Store: Record overall NotificationStatus
end

note over Adapter, Provider
  Adapter/provider pairs: Email, Slack, Teams.
  Select one pair per channel; new adapters
  preserve the handler's send flow.
  Success means provider acceptance,
  not confirmed receipt or reading by the user.
end note

@enduml
